                <mxCell id="DzvHcSQ4JyJ5foZKjtJD-14" value="&lt;b&gt;1. TS Data path tracks number of buffers passed to DMA post-GATE.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Event Engine has a configuration register to enable and disable Event sources and signals.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Event Engine can optionally receive event from Sync Input.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. Event Engine can optionally set output on Sync Output.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Event Engine can have an event set via an Event Generator controlled by the Host application.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. When Event Engine fires, latch the Buffer Count in a Event Buffer register and latch the Event Sample Offset register.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. The Event Source/Type and Event sample are pushed to an Event FIFO.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;8. TS Driver tracks counts number of buffers transferred.&amp;nbsp; Count should correlate to buffer counter in logic (#1).&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. Application can read from the Event FIFO to determine when an event has occurred.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Lucida Console;fontSize=16;textShadow=0;labelBorderColor=none;labelBackgroundColor=default;" parent="1" vertex="1">
